## 2. FEW-SHOT PATTERNS — Subject Line

### ❌ BAD: Subject uses dashes
```
Subject: WSR - 15-Jan-25 - Customer Portal - Green - NA
```
**Why wrong:** Parser expects pipes (`|`) as delimiters. Result → silent rejection.

### ✅ GOOD: Subject uses pipes + Status - prefix
```
Subject: WSR | 15-Jan-25 | Customer Portal | Status - Green | NA
```

### ❌ BAD: Missing `Status -` prefix
```
Subject: WSR | 15-Jan-25 | Customer Portal | Green | NA
```
**Why wrong:** Guidelines line 16 mandates `Status -` prefix verbatim.

### ❌ BAD: Slash date
```
Subject: WSR | 15/01/25 | Customer Portal | Status - Green | NA
```
**Why wrong:** Date must be `dd-mmm-yy` (line 14).

### ❌ BAD: Reply/Forward
```
Subject: Re: WSR | 15-Jan-25 | Customer Portal | Status - Green | NA
```
**Why wrong:** Any prefix other than `WSR | ...` breaks parsing (line 9-10). Always compose fresh.

### ✅ GOOD: Real-world (Heineken reference)
```
Subject: WSR | 10-Apr-26 | MS - PS - Heineken Legacy Migration-Project | Status - GREEN | EMEA North
```

