## 8. DECISION MATRIX — Ask vs Attention

| Item | Classification |
|------|----------------|
| "We need a decision from exec on X by Friday" | **Ask** (has owner + deadline) |
| "We need 2 more devs for sprint Y" | **Ask** (resource request) |
| "Blocker on test data — team notified, call scheduled" | **Attention** (FYI for leadership awareness) |
| "Risk of schedule slip due to external dep" | **Attention** (transparency) |
| "Leadership should escalate with Client X" | **Ask** (escalation request) |
| "Production incident resolved" | Neither — belongs in Summary/Completed |

### Rule of Thumb
- **Ask** = explicit request for leadership action (decision/resource/escalation), with owner + deadline
- **Attention** = awareness item; leadership should know but no action required from them

### Critical Blockers → BOTH
If a blocker is critical, put a brief note in Summary + detailed info in Attention.

