## 13. INFER-FIRST PATTERNS (v1.1)

The simplified flow's central rule: parse before asking, never re-ask data already inferred.

### Pattern A — Mode A (Reference) Workflow
```
USER: "Compose a WSR. Here's last week's email — {.eml or pasted text}"
AGENT (silent Phase 0):
  → invokes prior_email_parser.py
  → extracts: project name, region, sender, CC, status, all 6 sections, metrics, days
  → auto-injects today's date
  → builds draft state
AGENT (Phase 1 single batch):
  → renders all 6 inferred sections with [from reference] markers
  → asks: leaves, jira paste, free-form updates
  → runs bidirectional sycophancy guard preview
USER: replies once with everything
AGENT (Phase 2):
  → integrates updates, computes days+metrics, runs validators silently
  → presents final draft + validation summary + gap report
USER: "approved" → bundle written, session ends
```

### Pattern B — Mode B (Fresh) Workflow
```
USER: "Compose a fresh WSR for Project Alpha"
AGENT (silent Phase 0):
  → no parser invocation
  → auto-injects today's date
  → loads team-roster.yaml
  → builds skeletal draft state
AGENT (Phase 1 single batch):
  → asks: project name (if not given), region, sender, status colors,
          summary bullets, completed, in progress, ask, attention,
          leaves, jira paste / metric values
USER: replies once
AGENT (Phase 2): same as Pattern A
```

### Pattern C — Mode A with Screenshot Description
```
USER: "Compose WSR. I can't paste the prior email but here's a screenshot
       showing: Project = Heineken Migration, Status Green, Capacity 102/102, ..."
AGENT (silent Phase 0):
  → no .eml available; treats user's description as a structured reference
  → extracts what's described; marks rest as needing batch input
AGENT (Phase 1): asks for missing fields + leaves + jira + free-form
... continues as Pattern A
```

### Anti-Pattern — Re-Asking Inferred Data
```
❌ AGENT: "What's your project name?"  (when reference provided it)
✅ AGENT: "Project: MS - PS - Heineken Legacy Migration-Project [from reference]"

❌ AGENT: "What date is this WSR for?"
✅ AGENT: "Date: 22-Apr-26 [auto: today's date]"

❌ AGENT: per-section approval — "Is the Summary OK? ... now Completed? ... now In Progress?"
✅ AGENT: single batch with all 6 sections rendered at once
```

