## 14. JIRA PASTE PARSING PATTERNS (v1.1)

The Phase 1 batch consolidates 4 metric prompts into one Jira-paste / description prompt. `metrics_inference.py` recognizes:

### Free-text patterns
| User wrote | Inferred |
|------------|----------|
| `Capacity 102 / 102` | `capacity_actual=102, capacity_planned=102` |
| `capacity 95%` | `capacity_percent=95` (actual/planned LEFT for follow-up if needed) |
| `43 stories planned, 10 dev completed` | `story_planned=43, story_completed=10` |
| `Build 4 defects, SIT 2 defects, UAT 1 defect, PROD 0` | per-phase defect counts |
| `0 valid defects this sprint` | all-phase defects = 0 |

### Tabular paste patterns
```
Phase  | Days | Defects | DpD
Build  | 646  | 0       | 0.00
SIT    | 646  | 4       | 0.01
UAT    | 646  | 5       | 0.01
PROD   | 0    | 0       | 0.00
```
→ Per-phase days/defects/DpD parsed directly.

### Jira CSV / list patterns
```
ABC-123  Done    Story 5pt
ABC-124  Done    Story 3pt
ABC-125  In Progress  Story 8pt
```
→ Counts rows by status: `dev_completed = sum(status == "Done")`, etc.

### Confidence levels
- **HIGH** — explicit numbers (`Capacity 102 / 102`)
- **MEDIUM** — percentage only (`capacity 95%`) — agent will ask follow-up if planned/actual needed
- **LOW** — vague qualitative (`went well`) — falls back to `⚠️ MISSING — please provide capacity actual / planned`

